Lets the runtime ICU loader of SkUnicode use the ICU a platform gives apps.

Skia's runtime loader dlopens libicuuc.so and looks only for versioned names
(u_errorName_74). Neither works for an app:
  - Android: libicuuc.so is not an NDK library, so an app cannot dlopen it.
    The NDK library is libicu.so (API 31, Android 12), with unversioned names.
  - Windows: there is no runtime loader at all (BUILD.gn allows it only on
    Android and Linux). Windows 10 1903+ ships icu.dll, 1703-1809 icuuc.dll,
    both with unversioned names.

With this patch the loader tries libicu.so then libicuuc.so (icu.dll then
icuuc.dll on Windows), and for each name tries the unversioned symbol before
the versioned ones. The first symbol found pins the form, as before. A library
that lacks a required symbol is closed and the next one is tried. If none
works SkUnicodes::ICU::Make() returns nullptr, as it did before.

No ICU data ships with the package: the platform's ICU brings its own.

